          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">How Much Do You Actually Cut Per Year?</h3>
          <p>
            If your chainsaw use amounts to a few fallen branches after storms and the occasional pruning session, a compact battery saw in the 12-16 inch range is more than enough, and you'll appreciate the low maintenance every single time you pick it up. If you're processing multiple cords of firewood every fall or maintaining several acres of timber, the calculus shifts firmly toward gas, where sustained power and refuel-and-go convenience actually matter.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Do You Already Own a Battery Tool Platform?</h3>
          <p>
