          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">How Far Are You From an Outlet?</h3>
          <p>
            If every tree and branch you'll ever cut is within 100 feet of your house, a corded electric chainsaw genuinely deserves consideration — it's the cheapest option, has zero engine maintenance, and never runs low on charge. If you're working anywhere on a larger property, cord tethering rules this category out immediately.
