          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The <strong class="text-white">best chainsaw</strong> is the one matched to how much you actually cut, not the biggest or most powerful one you can afford. For most homeowners handling firewood, storm cleanup, and general yard work, the <strong class="text-white">EGO Power+ CS1800</strong> proves a battery chainsaw can genuinely replace gas without sacrificing performance. If you fell large trees or process serious firewood volume every season, the <strong class="text-white">Stihline MS 462 Pro</strong> or the heavy-duty <strong class="text-white">Stihline MS 500i Pro</strong> deliver the sustained power gas is built for.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
            Whatever saw you choose, remember that <strong class="text-white">the chain matters as much as the machine</strong>. Keep it sharp, keep it properly tensioned, wear real PPE every time, and never cut above shoulder height. Do that consistently and any saw on this list will serve you safely for years.
